We can also transfer data from one component to another component, like we are sending data from app component
to user component in this

<app-user [name] = "user.name"> : here we will send name as user.name, user we are reading from json file of users
to accept this name in user component we added @Input name!String;

in user component typescript file if we mark @Input({required: true}) then that property will be required when sending
data from other component

we can also use signals for input values from other component
i.e avatar = input<string>() or avatar = input.required() -- for required

Signals can't be updated where they are used as input

if we want to send some data from child component to parent in our case from user component to app component
then we can use
@Output() select = new EventEmitter(),
 and to send value we can use select.emit([anyValue])
and in the parent template we need to hand over this value in ts to do that: (select)="onSelectUser($event)"

we can also use
select = output<string>() under the hood output<string>() creates new EventEmitter()
